WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.440
- Hi, I'm Aria and I'm in Los Angeles.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.440
- Hi, I'm Aishwarya and I live in Mumbai.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.533
- My name's Luisa and I'm
live in Sao Paolo, Brazil.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.190
- My name is Red, I live in Tokyo.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.980
- Hi, I'm Saba and I live in Berlin.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.053
- I'm Giovanni and I'm from Mexico City.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:18.183
- I wanted to see what trash
looked like around the world.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.865
So I contacted six BuzzFeeders,
at offices around the globe

00:00:21.865 --> 00:00:24.660
to go about their week,
and throw away things

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.080
as they normally would,
and at the end of the week

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.410
to empty out their trash,
and just to sort it

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.793
and see what sort of
trash they're producing,

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.300
and how they could potentially
reduce their waste.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:37.743
- [Man] Whoa.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.590
- [Aishwarya] Let's put all
the plastic on one side.

00:00:42.036 --> 00:00:42.869
- Plastic.

00:00:43.557 --> 00:00:44.390
Plastic.

00:00:44.852 --> 00:00:45.685
Plastic.

00:00:47.592 --> 00:00:50.227
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:50.227 --> 00:00:51.060
- [Aria] So that's more plastic here.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:55.400
- Plastic, it just really
stinks a lot right now.

00:00:55.748 --> 00:00:58.395
- Make it stop, make it stop.

00:00:58.395 --> 00:01:00.645
Why is there so much trash?

00:01:07.121 --> 00:01:11.038
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:18.733 --> 00:01:21.063
I don't do any sorting stuff.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.550
- Here in Mexico, we don't
separate trash that often.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.460
Finally I take my trash
out, and it was weird for me

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.633
because it was like a weird week;

00:01:27.633 --> 00:01:30.580
because I invited some
friends and we have beers,

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:34.300
I eat a lot of chips, and I
realized I make a lot of trash.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.930
- I guess we don't really
realize how much trash

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:39.140
we do tend to gather and build
over the course of a week.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.070
And this was a week that I
would consider a light week,

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:43.440
in terms of me being at home.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.980
I didn't do very much at home.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.320
For a light week, I'd say
that's a fairly sizeable chunk.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:50.726
- Now honestly I'm very
surprised at all the plastic

00:01:50.726 --> 00:01:54.050
that I've collected, because
at home I'm not into packaged.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.390
Like I'm into a healthy lifestyle,

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:57.653
so at home I wouldn't collect a lot of,

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.683
packaged foods, and stuff
like that but I guess,

00:02:00.821 --> 00:02:03.720
I'm not as sustainable as I though I was.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.280
- There is lots of cat food wrappers and

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.130
ice cream wrappers too because

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.250
it was very hot these past days.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.083
Juice cartons.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:17.470
Also this packaging for
vegetables and salads, and grapes.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.940
I don't know if it's a lot.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.223
Some of it is probably not necessary.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.143
This is the waste that I've
produced during the week.

00:02:25.223 --> 00:02:26.070
In total, I think it is a lot.

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:29.220
And I think it wouldn't
be such a big problem

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.520
if we knew that all the recyclable parts

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.353
would be actually recycled.

00:02:35.517 --> 00:02:38.100
(gentle music)

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.490
- I guess I could
definitely work on myself.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.120
Less takeout, more cooking, but if I cook,

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.140
then I should also pay attention to how

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.570
the vegetables and the
salad and everything else,

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.730
all the ingredients are wrapped.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:53.903
You can do better, Saba,
is my conclusion to this.

00:02:54.241 --> 00:02:58.241
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:15.080
- Even if you don't
produce a lot of trash,

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.513
you can always reduce it.

00:03:16.597 --> 00:03:18.992
- When I buy a product,
I never think about

00:03:18.992 --> 00:03:20.783
the material it's made of.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:23.783
I mostly just think about my convenience.

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:28.050
And I feel like now, I'm gonna
be more aware and mindful

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.350
about the kind of trash I'm making.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:33.890
I think everyone should just
life one step at a time,

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:35.941
and if everyone does
it, then it's definitely

00:03:35.941 --> 00:03:38.543
gonna be a great, great future ahead.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:40.660
- Hey, Unsolved is on a new
channel, and now your part.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:41.720
- [Both men] Subscribe here.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:42.823
- That was my part.

